Subject: [PATCH 08/12] Plantard NTT: point at pqm4's existing UIC-ESLAS macros
 + diagnose representation gap
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two findings from looking at what pqm4 already ships:

1. crypto_sign/ml-dsa-{44,65,87}/m4f/{macros_smallntt.i,smallntt_769.S}
   already vendor the UIC-ESLAS Plantard NTT (Huang et al., TCHES
   2024). The macros file is fully register-parameterised so the
   asm template is reusable for HAWK; what needs to change is just
   the modulus immediate, the qa constant, the twiddle table, and
   the layer-merge unrolling for n=512 / n=1024.

2. tests/test_plant_twiddle.c simulates the asm mul_twiddle_plant
   macro in C and searches the encoding space against
   mq18433_montymul as the golden. Best candidate (twiddle encoded
   as ω·Q0I mod 2^32, qa=1<<16) misses ~51% of random (a, b) pairs
   in [1..Q]^2 — the gap is that smulwb does a SIGNED multiply with
   a SIGNED >>16 (Plantard's natural form), while HAWK's montyred is
   UNSIGNED throughout. Plantard's natural output range is roughly
   [-q, q]; HAWK keeps coefficients in [1..Q] because hawk_sign.c
   does mq18433_montymul/sub/tomonty on individual coefficients
   between NTT calls.

Two paths forward, documented in PLANTARD_NOTES.md:
  - Path A: run NTT in Plantard's centred form, normalise to [1..Q]
    once at NTT exit; mirrors ml-dsa. Faster, more intrusive.
  - Path B: bake conditional '+Q' into the inner butterfly so the
    running representation stays [1..Q]. Drop-in, ~1-2 extra
    cycles per butterfly.

Either choice keeps the locked-down Q0I and the existing GM[] table
(modulo the Plantard encoding step on table contents), and is
validated by the existing tests/test_plant_ntt.c byte-equality check.

Next step is a representation-choice decision; once that's made the
asm port is largely a translation of ml-dsa-44/m4f/smallntt_769.S
with the constant substitutions above and an extra layer-group for
the larger HAWK polynomial degrees.
